    {
      "name": "lagging-peer-blocks-reclamation",
      "description": "Same log, but a peer has only acknowledged the first op, so the horizon stops there. The first op is itself superseded AND below the horizon, so it goes; the second cannot, because a peer that has not yet seen the winner would be left with neither. One lagging peer is the difference between reclaiming two ops and reclaiming one. The peer is named in blockedBy, so a caller can see why reclamation stalled instead of watching the log grow with no explanation.",
      "ops": [
        {
          "id": "018bcfe56800-0000-29de64fc1545395ccd0586fefbda3a82",
