    {
      "name": "tombstone-gc-reclaims-the-whole-row",
      "description": "With includeTombstones, a tombstoned row below the horizon is removed entirely: the tombstone AND every cell op of that row, together. Dropping the tombstone while leaving the row's other cells would resurrect the row on the very next read, which is the failure this rule exists to prevent. The surviving row is untouched.",
